==German==

===Etymology===
From Late {{inh|de|gmh|pūr}} (14th c.), from {{der|de|la|pūrus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/puːr/|[pu(ː)ɐ̯]}}
* {{rhymes|de|uːɐ̯}}
* {{audio|de|De-pur.ogg|Audio}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|er|sten}}

# [[pure]], [[mere]], [[sheer]] {{gloss|nothing other than}}
#: {{syn|de|rein|blank|bloß|schier}}
#: {{ux|de|Die '''pure''' Verzweiflung hat ihn dazu getrieben.|It was '''pure''' despair that drove him into it.}}
#: {{ux|de|Köstliche Häppchen und erstklassiger Wein sorgten für Genuss '''pur''' in jeder Hinsicht.|Delicious snacks and first-class wine ensured '''pure, unadulterated''' pleasure in every respect.}}
# [[pure]] {{gloss|not mixed with another ingredient}}
#: {{syn|de|rein|unverdünnt|unvermischt}}
#: {{ux|de|Er trinkt '''puren''' Wodka.|He drinks '''pure''' vodka.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er trinkt Wodka '''pur'''.|He drinks vodka '''straight'''.}}
# {{lb|de|rare}} [[pure]] {{gloss|not polluted or sullied}}
#: {{syn|de|rein|sauber|schadstofffrei|unverdorben}}

====Usage notes====
* The construction "X[noun] {{m|de|pur}}," with the adjective {{m|de|pur}} uninflected and positioned after the noun, is used idiomatically in a sense of "pure and simple"
* As a more flexible equivalent for {{m+|en||pure}} use the adjective {{m|de|rein}}, especially in moral and other figurative senses.
* Due to the semantic constraints, the compared forms, especially the comparative {{m|de||purer}}, are infrequent.

====Declension====
{{de-decl-adj|pur|purer|purst}}

